Field 2: Loan Inquiry (Name)

This field already exists; it was created along with the object.

Fields & Relationships → click Loan Inquiry Name → Edit.
Field Label: Loan Inquiry. The type stays Text(80), which is fixed.
Save. The concatenation logic (Opp Type + Closing date) isn’t part of this step; it’s marked TBD in the story.

Field 1: Loan Inquiry Number

New → Auto Number.
Field Label: Loan Inquiry Number. Field Name: BKU_Loan_Inquiry_No.
Display Format: LI-{000000}. Starting Number: 1.
Leave “Generate Auto Number for existing records” unticked; there are no records yet.
Set FLS and layout, then Save & New. The field is read-only automatically.

Field 3: Loan Origination Source

New → Picklist.
Field Label: Loan Origination Source. Field Name: BKU_Loan_Origination_Source.
Choose “Enter values, with each value separated by a new line”:
   OnePath
   OPX
   Commercial Cards
Tick “Restrict picklist to the values defined in the value set.”
Set FLS and layout, then Save & New.

Field 4: Loan Stage

New → Picklist.
Field Label: Loan Stage. Field Name: BKU_Loan_Stage.
Enter the values in this order:
   Inquiry Submitted
   Proposal Issued
   Proposal Accepted
   Underwriting
   Submitted for Approval
   Approved
   Loan Closing
   Booking
   Booked
   WAR
   Paid off
Tick Restrict picklist.
Optionally, ask whether the default should be Inquiry Submitted. The story doesn’t say.
Set FLS and layout, then Save & New.

Field 7: Opportunity (master-detail)

New → Master-Detail Relationship → Related To: Opportunity.
Field Label: Opportunity. Field Name: BKU_Opportunity.
Sharing Setting: Read/Write. Users who can edit the Opportunity can then edit its Loan Inquiries.
“Allow reparenting”: leave it unticked for now and confirm with your lead.
Next → FLS. Master-detail fields are always required, so you only set visibility here. Then the layout.
Related list on Opportunity: the wizard asks which Opportunity layouts should get the Loan Inquiries related list. Untick all of them unless your lead says otherwise, because Opportunity has a lot of layouts.
Save.
Add the OnePATHE filter. Open the new Opportunity field → Edit → Lookup Filter → Show Filter Settings.
Criteria: Opportunity: Opportunity Record Type equals the 3 OnePATHE record types (New/Initial Funding; Pay-Down, Pay-Off or Advance; Renewal, Mod or Extension).
Filter Type: Required.
Error message: “Loan Inquiry can only be created for OnePATHE opportunities.”
Save.

Field 6: Deal

New → Lookup Relationship → Related To: PL Deal. Check its exact label in the list.
Field Label: Deal. Field Name: BKU_Deal.
Not required. If the lookup record is deleted: “Clear the value of this field.”
Set FLS and layout.
For the related list on Deal layouts, untick all for now. Save & New.

Field 8: Relationship

New → Lookup Relationship → Related To: Account. It may show as “Relationship” because Account is relabelled.
Field Label: Relationship. Field Name: BKU_Relationship.
Not required. If the lookup record is deleted: “Clear the value of this field.”
Set FLS and layout.
For the related list on Relationship layouts, untick all for now. Save & New.

Field 5: Amount

New → Formula.
Field Label: Amount. Field Name: BKU_Amount. Return Type: Currency. Decimal Places: 2.
Next → Advanced Formula and enter:
   BKU_Opportunity__r.Amount
Click Check Syntax. Blank Field Handling: “Treat blank fields as blanks.”
Set FLS and layout, then Save.
